{"title":"2026 MADE Rackspotting: Talisman Hunting in the Bike Valet – Spencer Harding","link":"https://theradavist.com/2026-made-rackspotting-talisman-hunting-in-the-bike-valet","date":1788246017000,"content":"<p><em>As we run down our <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/tag/2026-made-bike-show\" target=\"_blank\">2026 Made Bike Show</a> coverage, there’s one important part of the show we need to showcase: the bikes locked up at the show! Spencer took some respite from wandering the aisles of Zidell Yards to peruse the bike valet and racks outside the show, in search of talismanic bike nerdery. See what he found below…</em></p>\n<p><span></span></p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/91c956d6db57b4d8cb0cbdedd5fe05cd9989ba7fc33bb2ecef5d304e47af771b.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/a31d6abab56b908cbc55d0dcabbe27e6d7ec17299d9b3fcaab041a6f2879feb4.jpg 640w, /media/91c956d6db57b4d8cb0cbdedd5fe05cd9989ba7fc33bb2ecef5d304e47af771b.jpg 1800w, /media/7b8c14c447b33b876e10209d3d790e7ec02083719fdc381e9b2d52a0e585b38e.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>While listening to a recent episode of Ronnie and Arya’s <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/show/0s3SCSL8JBp4Hxv6rnez2F\">Alt Bike Now podcast,</a> they were discussing the idea of talismans in signaling to other bike nerds. White Industries hubs or cranks, Chris King headsets, obscure CNC parts from the 90s, Paul bits – you get the idea. How we decorate and accessorize our bikes is a reflection of our personality, our riding history, even our accolades.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/a066442ce77348b33991adadb1f0a6a30fcc1c2371d3299639e7fa40fcbd0792.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/f8d0cc2da78fb43964cce5956fe774ff3d689e0f71c3c4cd01c5a7f12704b976.jpg 640w, /media/a066442ce77348b33991adadb1f0a6a30fcc1c2371d3299639e7fa40fcbd0792.jpg 1800w, /media/b939939d425759affecfc7fea158a0da8fb53356471ee289bac4dc718e2fa294.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>I started wandering the bike racks the first year I went to the Made Bike Show as a way to find a new angle that wasn’t shooting the insane selection of bikes at the show. While there are quite a few bikes that came to the show well worn and ridden, most are waiting until after the show for a long-awaited spin and permission to get dirty. So I wandered the racks to see what the nerds had ridden to the show.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/9511853a46893298195b7fb8470f7e9e3731d6ea533faa30699080dbad5b8432.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/bfa9cd036748e4f85011abbae9c9d866735ad84d26a0fa321933e6e2623c579a.jpg 800w, /media/fe26c67d2345837bcf3889cacdd50e45ecd117d21d2ebf6681aa7d0b47bd6c34.jpg 1600w, /media/9511853a46893298195b7fb8470f7e9e3731d6ea533faa30699080dbad5b8432.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/98cd269367956c5d8d5cfbd85adcfa8980238194972c63878739e7605adb655a.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/b62eb4fccee1acdb906a86f5f956221f42e6f87c84187306899005b02c6525a6.jpg 800w, /media/48e66c031f67dab55a9e71a8708480d0b8c010bcbc28e702778e34065f07d9fd.jpg 1600w, /media/98cd269367956c5d8d5cfbd85adcfa8980238194972c63878739e7605adb655a.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Portland supports a wide range of bike nerdery, from the Grant Peterson Rivendell purists to those keeping track bikes relevant. It was heartwarming to see the spectrum of bikes that made their way to the show.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/e488db5932d81995a4e50abf8ee663c76da0ce3c8e95524315c2ee775ec2edda.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/97faf38cc27c9eb27f67f68a3a2e9805efd6b789796af2bbbd074bdf583fe34c.jpg 800w, /media/e488db5932d81995a4e50abf8ee663c76da0ce3c8e95524315c2ee775ec2edda.jpg 1600w, /media/d0d5983f8bc48b41f4a6d89a4cb1537ccc42372b73d325f2f54632619f74382f.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/0a38a02515592879b429ae63cc270ba6a4d4988ba7c2b10150d45a545f6c6100.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/80850af5ca431e81c849aa6c0829b41b92d224d58c2c962e0f807a6fb6698f99.jpg 800w, /media/0a38a02515592879b429ae63cc270ba6a4d4988ba7c2b10150d45a545f6c6100.jpg 1600w, /media/136584e4977e23a78b44b52bdd382e1c9baabc91a7d5704fff08c6e76f73669a.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/5211593472d73f174e207bbc1d785a7ccb7b10eff833b2110d65ed1e1a6c196b.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/70cf2400004ce7689dbb524c8d6134ce0262701a4dad3f77a5cf1b786463718a.jpg 800w, /media/5211593472d73f174e207bbc1d785a7ccb7b10eff833b2110d65ed1e1a6c196b.jpg 1600w, /media/5871b344807a6f50230ff6d6b18fa14c54b61b8d46f1619d2acc114e94680f2b.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>Track bikes had a particularly strong showing – there were a few Destroy bikes that I’d seen at the show in years past, clearly now being ridden regularly and not treated too carefully. One of my favorites was the red Ritchey track bike with cow print Outer Shell bags and one of the best chainrings I’ve ever seen. The fixed gear world is still going strong in Portland, and I’m here for it.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/b687cbefc720f708f4e8953bfb340e283d0f33c4cb22b55d7af56a5cd46ced69.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/680d9839f46e3d8b8467e519871b858743afc14bfd45f5dd9e962aa4526195c1.jpg 800w, /media/b687cbefc720f708f4e8953bfb340e283d0f33c4cb22b55d7af56a5cd46ced69.jpg 1600w, /media/20bfe343e4b9d3e1571a4efecb8f19383b160c00067b0545dcd430951d66bb2f.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/343d3207fd41621dac362ae7fb3e27240f22b16478d8f8fa51d7ea8f305b3222.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ee59be5e3db0871bc030f11cc49866fe180cb569b93281686174165fd980cc60.jpg 800w, /media/343d3207fd41621dac362ae7fb3e27240f22b16478d8f8fa51d7ea8f305b3222.jpg 1600w, /media/0671ca4e64cfdbcc0d548381205c30407267e50e2be6c7243f187fca0ed8ee65.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/6d1c3681866b3301492a501ddd1ea78f0c302148efdace71ee3ad20034e6e0d7.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/1c4f6c472cae4d462eb5518f582f555b9475f1341f1a5ff0c62ca5403689e2e0.jpg 800w, /media/6d1c3681866b3301492a501ddd1ea78f0c302148efdace71ee3ad20034e6e0d7.jpg 1600w, /media/7532a61cc00024320f737f5815d066739588830c6ebe05b146f3dc186b3a345c.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>To no one’s surprise, I found a plethora of Crust and Rivendells adorning the racks. Romanceurs, Hunquapillars, Roadunos, even a Toyo Atlantis. The Rivendell cult has clearly made Portland one of its urban outposts, and it seems to be doing quite well.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/bb498e0e8cd98ec12b506a38eea7cbd96c86b59878a1a6d3af3c41e043474b4b.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/47e227933cd901defdd1a74207b2869c727a68c476a6115bb3d22aab3744ec8a.jpg 800w, /media/bb498e0e8cd98ec12b506a38eea7cbd96c86b59878a1a6d3af3c41e043474b4b.jpg 1600w, /media/4e3fb25f49ef8360e42f52d1f59464d841e3b11838af59c66cf12b23494c8efc.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/d0901ef1c94c4cd97429679ca283aad98d84ddada3002cbf3038cdc216e9c044.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/773610a83eb66d3eb839fbfc99425e50376b9b4368699cd66e3cec4f00dbab41.jpg 800w, /media/d0901ef1c94c4cd97429679ca283aad98d84ddada3002cbf3038cdc216e9c044.jpg 1600w, /media/f17e0e969fcb6acfc8ca648179b80bf9077a7126e43f512a186da29b742cf737.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/bd700fd80870a53df5992e0c654c3deb40be7e7a4e4bd7f4d9bf9103a644fe78.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/dce1adf168aebe0bc3255d964c8b40e017f3a8c262c56aa29e48bb5f03dda779.jpg 800w, /media/bd700fd80870a53df5992e0c654c3deb40be7e7a4e4bd7f4d9bf9103a644fe78.jpg 1600w, /media/0c442ffc397f54b50b6a282c727215dab492111b621ba0794c5d20a479e0a442.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>I saw bikes from past and previous shows such as Breadwinner, Ahearne, Gunnar, Moné, Cielo, Weis, Tomii, Fat Chance, Rat King, Destroy, Fitz, Significant Other, and Squid. This is all to say I found the range and amount of custom bikes being ridden and even locked up at the show heartwarming.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/9606084f1d163d2bf60d59af6f917a3c9d535f10de24ef273fddfefece2503bf.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/0eddc815b11d0082e5bd4d5be1fcf5dc8ca4adc9ef207de367774334b6f1bd90.jpg 800w, /media/9606084f1d163d2bf60d59af6f917a3c9d535f10de24ef273fddfefece2503bf.jpg 1600w, /media/3efa16ac008f6f2778888c86fe07d88dfe41ac95f3d3d9e6bb3f0cfc62550999.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/44f7637b414887e0ddd082f7be5afd9cd5d0810b281ce12644557f624955b448.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/f33a38b52b3588a5852dfa9cbbb2f85739f8d55f7a471fbdcbb40a071cac1e04.jpg 800w, /media/44f7637b414887e0ddd082f7be5afd9cd5d0810b281ce12644557f624955b448.jpg 1600w, /media/f2f629b3ded5b80e4a2db95b250ba3cf257369d9211784ccab24497c59e7de84.jpg\" /><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/c89609a2d34bdb5147393a9bedc16db7fc1ba8722469866d1a18d146f21ffe3f.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/326eaa09d8678f9213899aa2648b9562479d14a78e4d6b415db608e00d2f6ce1.jpg 800w, /media/c89609a2d34bdb5147393a9bedc16db7fc1ba8722469866d1a18d146f21ffe3f.jpg 1600w, /media/27099b3987b3e08aebee7047a7126887eb1292e081300d8e7953423fd51e8b52.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>It is easy to get lost in the bubble of the Made show, especially when you look outside at the blinding sun after hours in the dim old building, but there is light out there, and people are actually riding the bikes from the show.</p>\n<p><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/media/2db2220f6e196bbb8c65f5d25cc05f85694d8e7ec678f354f49fa7c5e6c85cd3.jpg\" srcset=\"/media/ac3c9123245dbf37f1b6f2e35235f15868cf16622b72d0b2dfb858a00408672c.jpg 640w, /media/2db2220f6e196bbb8c65f5d25cc05f85694d8e7ec678f354f49fa7c5e6c85cd3.jpg 1800w, /media/d8dbdd34a5f2d67e7d32a2febc1feca7d31917da01c9cfb721481e91b78d9fd3.jpg\" /></p>\n<p>I hope next year I’ll get to see a few bikes from this year’s show dirty, scratched, and locked up outside the show…</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://theradavist.com/2026-made-rackspotting-talisman-hunting-in-the-bike-valet\">2026 MADE Rackspotting: Talisman Hunting in the Bike Valet</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://cms.theradavist.com/\">The Radavist</a>.</p>","author":"spencer harding","comments":"https://theradavist.com/2026-made-rackspotting-talisman-hunting-in-the-bike-valet#comments","siteTitle":"The Radavist","siteHash":"96eb481d8084f04a4602bac57874ba717baf56b758f45547b5caf2312da766ef","entryHash":"437839f903706f910d8088c60441761def0f3691973a83e2be7c859b01feb8ef","category":"Cycling"}